WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.330
The SCP Foundation contains a lot of monsters.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:11.720
From SCP-682, the lizard that refuses to die,
to SCP-939, a species of pack hunters that

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:16.590
steal the voices of their victims – the
dangerous predators that occupy the hundreds

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:22.490
of containment cells of the Foundation make
it their job to hunt and kill innocent people

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.490
– or worse.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.630
But have you ever wondered where some of those
monsters come from?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:34.639
The first encounter that the SCP Foundation
had with SCP-4049 was on July 14th of 2010.

00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:39.120
The Foundation operates a massive surveillance
network around the entire world – through

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:46.280
the use of AI, delegated duties, and compartmentalized
information, they’re able to have 911 operators

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:51.359
report any calls that seem anomalous in nature
while knowing nothing about the Foundation

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:52.459
itself.

00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:56.989
This way, they’re able to constantly be
aware of anything anomalous going on in the

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:00.010
country that gets reported to 911.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:05.079
On July 14th, the Foundation was alerted of
a call that likely had an anomalous component.

00:01:05.079 --> 00:01:07.810
At first, it didn’t seem like much.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:13.060
It was to a remote address in Wyoming, outside
of a small town called Gardnerville.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:18.740
The vacation home of one Richard Samson, a
wealthy businessman in the area, placed right

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.920
on the slopes.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.150
The call was made late in the afternoon, by
someone purporting to be the groundskeeper

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.979
of the home while Mr. Samson was away.

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:32.390
He was screaming into the phone, terrified
and largely incoherent, but the operator made

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.249
out something about a monster attacking the
house.

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:40.590
There was a lot of noise in the background,
sounds of shouting, destruction, and what

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.359
sounded like animalistic roars and grunts.

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:48.030
The 911 operator moved the call up, and it
didn’t take long for the Foundation to determine

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.509
that something strange was going on here.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:55.119
They dispatched a handful of agents, deep
undercover as officers with the Wyoming Highway

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:59.229
Patrol, to the address of the home where the
call had come from.

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:04.389
After about half an hour, the agents called
back in to HQ - the scene they had found was

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:06.929
nothing short of gruesome.

00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:11.039
Upon arrival, they were greeted with what
appeared to be the aftermath of a particularly

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:13.480
violent and brief tornado.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.190
The entire front section of the ground floor
had been shredded, the gardens trampled, and

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.620
the interior utterly destroyed.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:25.680
The agents picked their way between the wreckage
of the home – it functionally didn’t exist

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.680
anymore.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.260
The walls were collapsed from being rammed
and torn through, and the roof had collapsed

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.519
in on itself.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:37.220
The broken shards and pieces of furniture
and wreckage were everywhere.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:42.319
Despite appearances, this wasn’t a tornado
– a tornado would have thrown the entire

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:43.680
house around.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:52.239
No, this was as the groundskeeper had said
– something alive, monstrous, and very angry.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:56.520
Speaking of the groundskeeper, the Foundation
agents began to look for him once they took

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.970
stock of the damage to the home.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:03.159
At first, they couldn’t find him among the
massive pieces of debris and assumed the worst.

00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:07.620
Even if whatever had destroyed the house decided
to not kill him, he could easily have been

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:13.010
killed by the collapsing house, buried under
rubble, or a dozen other things.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:17.120
They picked through the ruins, calling out
that they were from the police and were here

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.160
to help.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.959
Eventually, after another half hour of searching,
they heard something.

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:26.120
What sounded like crying and whispering became
audible as the wind died down.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:30.310
The agents honed in on the noise and found
it was coming from one of the larger piles

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.360
of rubble.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.689
After getting some equipment, they were able
to heft up the piece of the collapsed roof,

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:41.040
and found the groundskeeper underneath, curled
into a ball and talking to himself.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.469
He seemed to be in some kind of a panicked
fugue state, not responding to the agents

00:03:45.469 --> 00:03:47.020
trying to get through to him.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:51.640
They wrapped him in a shock blanket and put
him in the back of one of their patrol cars,

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.319
but even after that they couldn’t get anything
of use out of him - he was just shaking and

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.750
muttering something about monsters.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:04.269
Eventually, he was given amnestics to forget
about the incident entirely and recovered.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:09.060
After the agents reported back to HQ, a new
issue popped up - they weren’t the only

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.920
ones who knew about this.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.290
A news website a few counties away had the
story.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:18.220
The Foundation quickly put out a cover story
- the house had probably been destroyed by

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.200
a group of grizzly bears, possibly rabid.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.590
They had the local government issue a warning
advising local residents to stay inside and

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:29.200
out of the wilderness until the animals could
be tracked and euthanized.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.000
And that’s exactly what the Foundation did.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:38.990
Mobile Task Force Epsilon-6, the Village Idiots
an MTF that specializes in taking on anomalous

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:44.590
threats in remote, rural areas and small towns
- were dispatched to track and contain or

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.700
terminate whatever had destroyed that mansion.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:52.990
The creature had left a strong trail of tracks,
scent, and general destruction, and the troopers

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:57.690
followed it north for hours, into another
dense forest – where they discovered the

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:02.620
gigantic, hulking creature while it was asleep
and shot it.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:08.080
It was huge, with rippling muscles on all
four legs and no fur to speak of – but the

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.560
most striking feature was a frighteningly
human face.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.840
The agents resolved to let the researchers
handle the autopsy, and busied themselves

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:21.410
with the other thing in that forest: there
was an old, abandoned arms factory that the

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.380
creature seemed to have come from.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:28.190
The agents descended into the decrepit, abandoned
building, following the creature’s trail

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.610
right into the basement.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:34.520
There, they found a large steel door, and
behind it, the anomaly that would eventually

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.580
be called SCP-4049.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:43.470
It was strange – it seemed to be some kind
of massive, empty room looking up into the

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:46.620
sky, even though they were deep underground.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:51.830
Not entirely empty - the dirt ground had a
series of concentric rings of gravestones

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.960
in it, all facing inward.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.080
The agents retreated once they realized they
had walked into a spatial anomaly and called

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.160
for backup.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.980
The Foundation quickly flew in researchers
and a containment team to figure out what

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:07.730
the anomaly was and to ensure no one else
got into the factory while they figured that

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:08.730
out.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.120
The basement of the factory became a sort
of base of operations for the large crew of

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:17.000
research and security personnel assigned to
SCP-4049.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:23.270
After making sure there were no other of the
monsters, designated SCP-4049-1 instances,

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:27.250
in the nearby forest, the researchers began
to experiment on it.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:32.190
They determined that the room on the other
side of the hallway was in an extradimensional

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.190
space.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:37.210
Members of D-Class personnel were sent in
with GPS trackers and even though they could

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:41.470
still be heard fine on the radio, the GPS
trackers failed totally.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:46.520
Obviously, the fact that you could see the
sky from an underground room was anomalous,

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:51.020
but attempts to dig into where the room should’ve
been from the surface also led to nothing

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.470
but more dirt.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.020
From inside, the D-Class members were able
to give a detailed report on the room as they

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.020
walked around.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:02.430
It was perfectly circular and pretty large
- about 30 feet across, give or take.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.770
A tall white wall ringed the room’s border
and was perfectly smooth and impossible to

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.360
get a grip on enough to climb – cold, hard
marble.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.610
The floor of the room wasn’t marble, though
– it seemed to be regular dirt.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:20.620
The D-Classes were ordered by researchers
to get samples of what they could, and they

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.740
scooped a little dirt into sample bags.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:28.740
But as soon as the subjects stepped back over
the threshold into the corridor of SCP-4049,

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:34.580
the sample bags they collected spontaneously
combusted, going up in flames.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:39.500
Any chemical analysis of its composition was,
of course, impossible.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:43.660
The researchers resolved to get what information
they could out of just looking at SCP-4049

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:44.660
first.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.520
And there was still a lot to look at.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:53.330
The D-class inspected the rings of gravestones
inside SCP-4049 – there were just two at

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.780
the moment, a larger ring containing a smaller
ring.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:01.140
Inside the smaller ring, there was a circular
empty space a few feet wide.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:06.120
Most of the graves were unfilled and unmarked
– just a patch of dirt turned over.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:10.900
But about a dozen of them had a gravestone
at their head, made of that same white marble

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.280
substance the walls were made from.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:18.970
They weren’t fancy – just a simple white
rectangle, stamped with some strange symbols.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:23.550
The D-class took photos and sent them to the
researchers, who recognized the markings as

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.280
a word in Ancient Greek: “hound”.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:31.870
The researchers were admittedly baffled by
what this could mean for SCP-4049, but decided

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:39.289
to figure out the connection using the evidence
they had: the corpse of the SCP-4049-1 instance.

00:08:39.289 --> 00:08:44.399
The researchers placed the huge corpse inside
the factory, creating a secure space to perform

00:08:44.399 --> 00:08:45.399
the autopsy.

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:51.250
Then, a team of doctors began cutting into
it with scalpels - or they tried, anyway.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:55.139
They quickly realized that the skin of the
creature was far too thick to be breached

00:08:55.139 --> 00:08:58.920
with scalpels, and resorted to long, sharpened
knives.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:03.550
They discovered quite a few things about the
instance's anatomy, along with why and how

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.850
it was able to do and absorb so much damage.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:10.089
It was a quadruped, walking on four limbs.

00:09:10.089 --> 00:09:14.709
The forward ones seemed to be in the shape
of arms with elbows and wrists, but also had

00:09:14.709 --> 00:09:16.990
clawed paws like a dog’s.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:22.769
The back legs were thick and heavily muscled,
and digitigrade - again, just like a dog,

00:09:22.769 --> 00:09:26.620
so they could be used to leap and jump great
distances.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:30.800
Once they cut away the skin, the researchers
noticed that it was indeed much thicker than

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:37.410
they expected it to be – human skin is only
about 2mm thick, but this was a full centimeter

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.670
throughout, as well as incredibly tough and
gamey.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:45.730
Internally, the structure was all wrong – it
seemed almost human-like, but with a few key

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.750
differences to suit the vastly-changed exterior
body.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:55.000
The spine was much thicker and wider, as well
as being curved to fit the four-legged structure.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.910
There seemed to be redundant organs – the
researchers theorized they were backups, like

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.870
the secondary heart they found inside the
creature’s innards.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:08.040
It could serve as a backup if the main heart
stopped working or was damaged, or it could

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.660
work together with the main heart to improve
the instance’s performance during physical

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:13.660
activity.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:18.220
There didn’t seem to be any kind of reproductive
system – it wasn’t surgically removed,

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:22.459
it just wasn’t there at all, like it had
magically disappeared.

00:10:22.459 --> 00:10:25.930
And inside the thing’s head, the skull was
different.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:30.499
The mouth was much wider and larger, and it
didn’t take long for the researchers to

00:10:30.499 --> 00:10:31.810
figure out why.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:37.439
When rooting around in its mouth, they quickly
discovered it had an extra set of sharp teeth

00:10:37.439 --> 00:10:39.490
behind its main set.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:44.149
All unnerving, slightly disturbing discoveries,
but the most frightening wasn’t something

00:10:44.149 --> 00:10:46.589
they found inside the instance.

00:10:46.589 --> 00:10:52.069
It was something they noticed immediately
upon containing it – its face was human.

00:10:52.069 --> 00:10:57.320
It had been morphed, of course, to fit the
altered skull, but there were two eyes, a

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:02.920
forehead, a nose, lips – it was inarguably
a human face.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:07.839
When the researchers sent for a DNA test,
they were disturbed but not surprised to discover

00:11:07.839 --> 00:11:13.230
what they had already been expecting: the
instance was entirely genetically human.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:19.329
Not a changed species or close relative – this
creature had once been a regular human being,

00:11:19.329 --> 00:11:20.839
like you or I.

00:11:20.839 --> 00:11:24.930
The researchers had just sent the DNA sample
off to check if there was a match in the criminal

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:29.829
database when suddenly, the lights went red,
the doors sealed, and the site’s alarms

00:11:29.829 --> 00:11:30.870
began to sound

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:38.870
At that moment, the steel door leading to
SCP-4049 flung open, and another SCP-4049-1

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:42.019
instance bounded out into the corridor on
all fours.

00:11:42.019 --> 00:11:46.220
It set its beady eyes on three members of
the Mobile Task Force, standing on the far

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.379
side of the long corridor.

00:11:47.379 --> 00:11:52.899
For a moment, it didn’t do anything – then
it let out a long screech that echoed around

00:11:52.899 --> 00:11:54.740
the entire factory.

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.399
Its rear legs tensed up, and it began to bound
down the hallway towards them.

00:11:58.399 --> 00:12:02.699
All of the security guards opened fire with
their machine guns on the anomaly, trying

00:12:02.699 --> 00:12:03.800
to bring it down.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:08.980
It shrugged off the bullets like they were
raindrops and didn’t so much as slow down.

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:13.070
Meanwhile, the two dozen other security personnel
in the facility were rapidly grabbing their

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:17.680
weapons and armor from their lockers before
rocketing down the stairs to the corridor.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:22.759
By the time they made it down, it was too
late – the instance was using its claws

00:12:22.759 --> 00:12:28.200
and jaws to tear two of the three poor members
of the Task Force to shreds.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.990
It wasn’t eating them - but it was attacking
them with enough anger and malice that there

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:35.579
wasn’t going to be much left when it was
done.

00:12:35.579 --> 00:12:40.470
The third member of the task force had fallen
and was backing away from the anomaly in fear.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:45.699
The remaining members of the Task Force opened
fire, smothering the SCP-4049-1 instance in

00:12:45.699 --> 00:12:47.240
a hail of bullets.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:51.970
The sudden, overwhelming firepower caught
it off-guard, and after a few seconds of sustained

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:55.110
gunfire, it fell to the ground, dead.

00:12:55.110 --> 00:13:00.279
Once the Foundation realized the active danger
that SCP-4049 presented, they decided not

00:13:00.279 --> 00:13:02.749
to take any chances with containment.

00:13:02.749 --> 00:13:08.420
The 50 meter long corridor leading to SCP-4049
from the basement elevator was fortified - an

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:13.139
airlock was installed on the far side, separating
it from the rest of the factory.

00:13:13.139 --> 00:13:17.749
Then motion detectors were set every few meters
throughout the hallway, attached to a series

00:13:17.749 --> 00:13:19.730
of ‘deterrents’.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:25.509
If an SCP-4049-1 instance smashed out of the
steel door, it would trip the alarms and activate

00:13:25.509 --> 00:13:31.089
everything from a supersonic sound cannon
to sentry guns and a machine gun emplacement.

00:13:31.089 --> 00:13:36.639
And if none of those worked, the entire corridor
could be pumped full of nerve gas, guaranteeing

00:13:36.639 --> 00:13:40.470
the death of the instance without risking
the lives of any personnel.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:45.680
This ‘kill corridor’ was to be guarded
by the Applied Task Force Iota-9 to ensure

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:50.730
that no SCP-4049-1 instance would survive
its escape.

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:55.269
But after the corridor was retrofitted, the
Foundation had a bigger problem: where were

00:13:55.269 --> 00:14:00.379
these SCP-4049-1 instances coming from to
begin with?

00:14:00.379 --> 00:14:04.959
They performed another DNA test on the new
instance – its face was different, so it

00:14:04.959 --> 00:14:07.089
seemed logical that it was a different person.

00:14:07.089 --> 00:14:12.220
When the results came back, the researchers
were surprised to find that not just one but

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:16.529
both of the samples had DNA matches in the
national database.

00:14:16.529 --> 00:14:20.460
Both were men from the tri-state area who
had mysteriously died or disappeared in the

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:24.559
past few months, while at some kind of religious
service.

00:14:24.559 --> 00:14:29.149
They were both avid big game hunters, with
an interest in shooting moose, bears, and

00:14:29.149 --> 00:14:30.149
elk.

00:14:30.149 --> 00:14:34.600
And most important, they had both been the
subject of a fire-related incident – one

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.559
had been presumed dead when his house burned
down.

00:14:37.559 --> 00:14:42.370
The other had simply vanished, with his car
being found hours later on fire by the side

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:43.370
of the highway.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:48.629
In both cases, a body was never recovered
- but the authorities did find a strange stone-tipped

00:14:48.629 --> 00:14:51.240
arrow driven into the ground nearby.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:54.869
Over the following months, the Foundation
observed a number of these strange events

00:14:54.869 --> 00:15:01.140
happen in Wyoming, Idaho, and Montana, and
like clockwork, every time it happened, a

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:09.199
new headstone appeared over one of the previously-unmarked
graves inside SCP-4049, saying the same Greek

00:15:09.199 --> 00:15:10.899
word: “hound”.

00:15:10.899 --> 00:15:15.529
On top of all of that, almost every time a
man in the area disappeared under these specific

00:15:15.529 --> 00:15:23.699
circumstances and a grave was created, an
SCP-4049-1 instance would appear inside SCP-4049

00:15:23.699 --> 00:15:28.890
sometime in the following two months, buried
within the soil circle in the center of the

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:29.890
room.

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:33.170
It would claw its way out of the dirt, smash
open the steel door to SCP-4049, and race

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:39.889
down the hallway trying to kill and destroy
whatever was in front of it until it was gunned

00:15:39.889 --> 00:15:40.889
down.

00:15:40.889 --> 00:15:43.940
But in one instance, that didn’t happen.

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:49.309
On September 17th of 2015, the Foundation
had gotten into the rhythm of containing SCP-4049,

00:15:49.309 --> 00:15:54.610
so they weren’t startled or caught off guard
when an agent with the Highway Patrol reported

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:59.379
finding a flaming truck near a hunting ground
– in the bed was an elk carcass, with a

00:15:59.379 --> 00:16:02.430
stone-tipped arrow lodged deep into the meat.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:06.860
Applied Task Force Iota-9 at the factory began
to prepare for an imminent appearance from

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:12.689
an SCP-4049-1 entity within the following
weeks, and established a round-the-clock guard

00:16:12.689 --> 00:16:14.240
in the kill corridor.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.240
But…

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.399
it never came.

00:16:16.399 --> 00:16:18.920
By December, nothing had happened at all.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:24.480
The Foundation made the decision – a D-class
would be sent into SCP-4049 with a camera

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:29.119
and radio, in the hopes of manually initiating
the event to occur.

00:16:29.119 --> 00:16:33.939
The D-class subject wasn’t given very specific
instructions - just fitted with a body camera,

00:16:33.939 --> 00:16:38.670
a two-way radio, and told to listen to all
instructions on his headset.

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:42.720
The researchers ordered him forward until
he reached the other side of the hallway,

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:48.600
where he was to open the steel door leading
to SCP-4049 and enter.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:53.610
When he entered, everything looked the same
as the Foundation expected it to - the same

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.209
gravestones, walls, and dirt.

00:16:55.209 --> 00:16:59.870
He moved towards the center of the room, to
the dirt circle, but suddenly stopped, looking

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:00.870
around.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:05.440
When the researchers asked why, he reported
hearing the sounds of dogs barking for a moment,

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:08.050
before the researchers told him to keep walking.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:12.670
When he stopped in the center of the room,
he again radioed in, feeling that someone

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.710
was there.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:18.760
The camera didn’t pick anyone up, but he
insisted that there was an odd feeling, just

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.500
before his audio stream suddenly cut out.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:27.040
A burst of static interference drowned everything
else out, and slowly winded down.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:33.110
The D-class couldn’t be heard anymore – but
a strange female voice was on the line, speaking

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.570
to the Foundation.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:39.630
She mentioned that the Foundation had been
ruining her pets for far too long.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:44.550
The Foundation demanded the speaker identify
themself, but she just scoffed, indignant

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:47.230
at what she called ‘human arrogance’.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:51.280
Right after that, all audio feeds were cut
out permanently.

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:56.580
This mysterious woman was designated SCP-4049-2.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:18:05.210
Seven seconds after they cut out, the largest
SCP-4049-1 instance ever recorded exited SCP-4049,

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.460
standing at almost 11 meters high.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:12.890
All of the deterrents were activated, but
even then, it still took all of them combined

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:17.430
with machine-gun fire from the Applied Task
Force to bring the creature down.

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:21.500
No remains of the D-class and no traces of
whoever was speaking on the radio were ever

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.980
found by the Researchers.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:27.840
It can be dangerous to stand between someone
and their beloved pets…

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:34.700
Now go watch “SCP-1437 - A Hole To Another
Place” and “SCP-087 - The Stairwell”

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:37.750
for more extradimensional spaces from SCP
Explained!

